            <span>Hi there!</span>
            <span>There is a particular kind of quiet that only happens in a kitchen — steam rising off a pot, the small sound of a knife against a board, light coming in slow through the window like it has nowhere else to be.
The Gentle Kitchen lives in that quiet .<br>
<br>It began, simply, from wanting food to feel like a homecoming rather than a performance. A bowl of something warm at the end of a long day. Rice beside butter. Broth beside bread. Two ways of eating that were never meant to compete, only to sit at the same table and keep each other company.</span>
            <br><span>There is no rush here. No plating for an audience, no dish trying to prove itself. Just the kind of cooking that happens when the house is quiet and the only thing asking for your attention is the pot on the stove.</span>
<br>
<span>Some evenings it feels like walking into a small clearing in a forest — nothing dramatic, just light falling differently, air a little softer, the sense that you're allowed to slow down.
If you've ever wanted your kitchen to feel that way too, you're in the right place.</span>
            <br><span>Welcome to The Gentle Kitchen.</span>
